# Cursor optimization

Keep this as a short operations guide. Put long tutorials in `documentation/`.

## Session context hygiene

- Prefer precise `@` references to relevant files over broad repo prompts.
- Keep `.cursorignore` / `.cursorindexingignore` current to avoid indexing build artifacts and generated output.
- Start a new chat for unrelated tasks to reduce stale context carry-over.

## MCP usage

- Daily default should stay lightweight: `github`, `linear`, `slack`.
- Enable high-footprint servers (AWS suites, analytics suites) only when the task explicitly needs them.
- Avoid duplicate connector sources (project MCP + plugin for the same service).
- Keep local server package versions pinned for reproducibility; avoid unbounded `@latest` in long-lived configs.

## Verification feedback loop

- Use native lint diagnostics and project scripts (`make lint`, `pnpm check`, targeted `pytest`) after edits.
- Fix newly introduced errors before expanding scope.

